// The walkgait package: a phase-driven biped walk with feet planted on the
// ground, an idle layer (breathing, weight shift) and a hard-landing crouch,
// for the 19-bone humanoid of the bonepose package. A program reaches it
// with 'import walkgait', makes a 'Walker' for a being's height, and each
// step calls 'Walker.update', which writes the being's pose.
//
// How it walks (the formulas and their sources are in gait.cone):
//
// - One phase, in cycles, advances by the DISTANCE the being travels divided
//   by its stride length, so a faster walk takes longer, slower steps and the
//   feet never skate: a foot in stance is held at a point of the ground, not
//   carried by the body. The left foot's phase is the cycle's, the right
//   foot's half a cycle on. A foot is down for the duty factor's share of
//   the cycle (about 0.62 walking, less running) and swings for the rest.
// - A foot's ground contact rolls: the heel strikes (toe up 12 degrees), the
//   foot goes flat, then the heel lifts and the ankle goes over the ball.
//   The ankle's travel along the ground is the stride's stance less that
//   roll, which is what keeps a step within a leg's reach.
// - When a foot starts to swing the ground height is asked of the caller at
//   the point it will land, so the walk follows the ground.
// - The pelvis is as high as both legs allow (97 per cent of full reach), so
//   it dips in double support and rises over the stance foot by itself; it
//   sways, turns and tilts a little with the stride, the chest turns the
//   other way, the arms swing against the legs.
// - Two-bone inverse kinematics (bonepose) reaches each ankle to its place.
// - Stopped, the walker finishes two more steps (each landing beside the
//   pelvis) and then stands with both feet flat; turning on the spot steps.
//
// Conventions are bonepose's: metres, y up, a being faces -z at yaw 0 and a
// positive yaw turns it left.
//
//   walkgait.cone   this overview
//   gait.cone       the gait's numbers and the stride, duty and roll
//   walker.cone     Walker, its feet and its update

mod walkgait;

import libc;
import collections use *;
import geomath use *;
import bonepose use *;
